 "not_established": [
  "why zjs is still ~2.0x qjs on new Uint8Array(64) after the probe is removed: that residual is spread across stages (view wrapper 2.57x, zero fill 4.28x, plain construct 2.03x, out-of-line 64-byte buffer 1.99x) and is not concentrated anywhere",
  "why new Uint8Array(existingBuffer) costs zjs 2.0 glibc mallocs and 2.0 arena events per operation while qjs costs 0.0004",
  "why a 440-object resident population makes zjs ~1800 instructions per operation more expensive with the probe off while it makes qjs ~1309 cheaper",
  "engine-internal object-creation counts: the ReleaseFast build reports all memory counters as 0 and instrumenting them would require touching src/, which Phase 1 forbids; only glibc allocation counts and bytes were measured dynamically",
  "zjs memset bytes: zjs issues no libc memset call at any size, so the zero fill is inline and invisible to the counter; the qjs column is real (64.1 B/op at ta64)",
  "the cost of the probe on a host where /sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max exists: there the open succeeds and the read is real, which was not measured",
